<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carausius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 293</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carausius was a Roman military commander of Menapian origin who was given command of the Channel fleet against Frankish and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">pirates</a> around 285. Accused of keeping captured plunder, he declared himself emperor in 286 and ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and part of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> until he was murdered in 293 by his finance minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allectus">Allectus</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carausius.jpg" alt="Carausius" width="320" height="147" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antoninianus_Carausius_leg4-RIC_0069v.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
